Overlay patch 0044 (visionOS Phase 01): no ENABLE_OPENGL on visionOS
(reference 0023 pattern). GLES does not exist on visionOS — gfx_opengl.cpp
cannot compile there; Metal is the only backend. iOS keeps GLES as a
debugging comparator. Every ENABLE_OPENGL consumer in LUS self-guards, so
the define simply evaporating is safe.

--- a/libultraship/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/libultraship/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -251,7 +251,7 @@
     endif()
 else()
     target_compile_definitions(libultraship PRIVATE
-        ENABLE_OPENGL
+        $<$<NOT:$<BOOL:${GS_VISIONOS}>>:ENABLE_OPENGL>
         $<$<CONFIG:Debug>:_DEBUG>
         $<$<NOT:$<CONFIG:Debug>>:NDEBUG>
         SPDLOG_ACTIVE_LEVEL=${SPDLOG_MIN_CUTOFF}
